{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet","id":954321,"title":"Honest Question - What do you think about Disquiet?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-20T05:48:11-07:00","id":954321,"title":"Honest Question - What do you think about Disquiet?","content":"So, here's the thing. Its been a while since I played Promethean its been years since the first edition came out and I played it. Now, after reading through the 2nd edition, I found myself becoming highly uncomfortable with Disquiet. Not because it isolated the Promethean, or drove them to do something, but because it felt too much like some variation on victim blaming.<br /> <br /> Prometheans are disfigured. They're a bit unbalanced mentally (unbalanced humors and all that). Fair enough. And everyone hates them because of all this - flaring disfigurements leads to more prejudice. It is literally is the Promethean's fault that everyone hates them. To me, I'm left feeling like we're just making an excuse for what amounts to prejudice and discrimination against the disabled. And I am not okay with that. <br /> <br /> I'm not the only one who feels that way, but, by the same token, there's a lot of people who feel radically different on the issue. So, here's my question. How do you feel about the issue? What do you take away from Disquiet? What do you think it means beyond a method of socially isolating the Prometheans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T05:52:37-07:00","id":954323,"title":"","content":"It's not the Promethean's &quot;fault&quot; that they engender Disquiet. It's something that they can't help. There's no moral judgement implied by it, it's just the unfortunate reaction between the Divine Fire and...basically everything else, but human perceptions in this specific case. <br /> <br /> It is, however, profoundly unfair, that much is true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T06:08:31-07:00","id":954332,"title":"","content":"Matt, I respect you, so don't take this wrong way, but that is nothing more than quibbling over semantics and doesn't actually answer the question. No, its not the Promethean's &quot;fault&quot; anymore than someone who's born with stunted arms are at fault for being born that way, or suffering an injury in combat, or anything like that. However, unlike someone who has these actual problems in real life, the problem entirely lies within the person with the actual prejudice. Or perhaps society itself teaching the person that prejudice. But in the case of Promethean, its specifically an attribute of the Created that fucks with people's minds and <i>forces them </i>to feel that way. All these games are metaphors, and the metaphor here is that the disfigurements are at fault for making people hate you. No, its not the prejudiced person's fault, its entirely you and your body's. And I'm not okay with that.<br /> <br /> This is my interpretation of the work, and people trying to just refute how I feel about it isn't going to be constructive; rather, that has the effect of actually <i>entrenching</i> people, myself included. I'm looking to hear other interpretations and ideas, specifically because that's how I learn and grow and get new perspectives. New ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T06:49:03-07:00","id":954349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=954332#post954332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the metaphor here is that the disfigurements are at fault for making people hate you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's where your metaphor breaks down for me. Because Disfigurements are only a part of what causes the Disquiet. Normal interactions also causes it, Failing a power also does. Being in your wasteland can cause such a thing too. Having a very disquieted friend can cause you to suffer disquiet.<br /> <br /> Promethean is about handicapped people, yes. But it's also about trans people, about autism, about sexuality, about homelessness, Promethean is about accepting yourself, and until then, others won't accept you.<br /> <br /> Have you ever had a friend always saying that no one loves them? That no matter what they do, they'll end up alone and sad? At first, you feel empathy, you want to help them, you give them support. Then you start to answer mechanically, without real thought. Then you start to tell them to stop complaining all the time, even if that's not really what you meant. And after some time, you need a breather, away from that person.<br /> <br /> While presiding over my game club, we've had a few people on the autism spectrum. One of them was higher on it than others. At first we tried to be inclusive, but at some point we had to have an intervention, because his presence demanded a lot from us, which we couldn't always provide.<br /> <br /> I've once met someone who has OCD about the *shhhh* sound. It caused him to get very aggressive. Like... <i>very</i> aggressive. He was expelled from college for assaulting his teacher. At first we tried our best, but once he decided to stay at the club and watch an RPG session we were playing (wihch is fine). He was on the couch, listening, basically being invisible, and at some point I roleplayed the sound of Acid melting metal, which, you guessed it, triggered him. Small events like these add up to people's tolerance of others and eventually we told him that he could either accept the noises we made in our private games or leave.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is... Disquiet is not the Promethean's fault. It's not the mortal's fault either. It's wrong alchemy between the two of them, causing the disquieted people to act out-of-character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T07:04:00-07:00","id":954357,"title":"","content":"It's an aspect of the Divine Fire, not the Created. It wears on the Promethean, producing Torment. It wears on the bystander, producing Disquiet. It wears on the world in general, producing the Wasteland. (It's the &quot;society&quot; in your comparison, perhaps).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T07:27:05-07:00","id":954367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=954332#post954332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]<br /> This is my interpretation of the work, and people trying to just refute how I feel about it isn't going to be constructive; rather, that has the effect of actually <i>entrenching</i> people, myself included. I'm looking to hear other interpretations and ideas, specifically because that's how I learn and grow and get new perspectives. New ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's actually your interpretation, there's little we can do for you. That's pretty much set on a bias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:56:03-07:00","id":954456,"title":"","content":"Jeez, what do you want? This is a game about being the Other, which cannot happen if Prometheans are not othered. It's about microaggression escalating into actual aggression and violence. Hell, it's even about &quot;entrenchment&quot;, because a Promethean's attempts to confront Disquiet directly just make it worse. <br /> <br /> Is Disquiet a metaphor? Yes. God yes. Does it excuse real world discrimination? No, not even. The Disquieted have as much choice in the matter as the Promethean inflicting it. IRL, people DO have a choice to overcome their conditioning, as there's no mystical obsession forced upon them. And, yeah, a lot of people would behave almost as badly without Disquiet, but that just tells you how bullshit an excuse Disquiet provides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:19:14-07:00","id":954473,"title":"","content":"When I think Disquiet, I specifically think of the scene in Frankenstein where the creature is talking to the old man in his house until his kids come home and everyone loses their shit and drives him off. Or the entire arc of Victor reacting with revulsion to his creation beyond the point of reason, and the drama that comes from that. I don't map it too closely to actual real-world prejudice, it's a clearly supernatural effect that has more to do with general fear and distrust of strangers than, for example, ableism specifically.<br /> <br /> For comparison: I've been running and playing Changeling for a long time, and endless digital ink has been spilled about the idea that C:tL is really specifically an allegory about abuse and trauma and recovery- and indeed, 2nd edition has been leaning hard into that angle. Personally, I don't really share that view and don't highlight it in my games. I see Changeling as primarily a modern urban fantasy/horror setting with its own specific vocabulary and ideas and building blocks that exist within the game world as just things in themselves. True Fae are in some ways evocative of abusers, but primarily they're alien dream monsters with magical powers that the players are fighting against.<br /> <br /> Bringing this back to Promethean, this game is a setting with its own rules and vocabulary as well. Disquiet is primarily a supernatural effect caused by Azoth, which is not a phenomenon that exists in reality and is necessarily going to be made up for drama and the group's enjoyment. The setting concept and game mechanic of Disquiet exists to create situations in play where the PCs have to either avoid/be cautious around human NPCs or deal with suspicion and angry mobs, which will ideally be fun and interesting to play out. It's on the ST to represent that suspicion in a more stylized or comic book-y way and not recreate actual real world prejudice.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I will now make the opposite of my previous point.<br /> <br /> Junot Diaz has said some really interesting things about sci-fi and fantasy drawing on real world experiences, one of which amounted to &quot;the X-Men setting idea and character beat that people 'hate and fear mutants' is derived from the actual history of racism, xenophobia, etc. X-Men would not make sense or even have been written in a world without racism, because that setting idea is a fictionalized and abstracted version of the actual reality and manifestations of racism.&quot; And so for example, people of color are inherently part of and suggested by X-Men stories, even when all the characters in a story are depicted as white and seemingly wouldn't be affected by real world racism.<br /> <br /> I don't think it was by Diaz, but I've also read analysis of how American popular sci-fi of the 50s-60s written by white male authors especially liked to present fantastic prejudice applying to white male characters who would be relatable to their primary intended audience. Like there's the character of the &quot;freak&quot;, the main character with some horrible disfigurement or physical trait that tragically isolates them from society, who is usually depicted as a white man. Twilight Zone, a great source for Promethean inspiration, has many examples of this. The original Doom Patrol comic is very explicitly about outcast &quot;freaks&quot; in a more nebulous and vague way than the setting-specific &quot;mutants&quot; of X-Men.<br /> <br /> Here's what I'm driving at with all this. I would argue that the authors of that brand of sci-fi were writing for an intended audience of people who did not themselves experience real-world racism, ableism, etc. The idea of a Twilight Zone story with a &quot;freak&quot; character isn't to evoke sympathy with &quot;I have felt that way and been mistreated by majority society too,&quot; but &quot;imagine if unfair and irrational prejudice happened to a normal person like you!&quot; Or maybe to imagine real-world prejudice in a safe, dramatized way that makes an interesting story, rather than a persistent mundanely dangerous reality.<br /> <br /> This applies to how Promethean as a fictional setting presents Disquiet. I don't know (seriously, I don't know the life stories of the writers) whether the Disquiet concept is particularly written by or for people who actually experience ableism themselves, to refer back to MCN's specific point. The fictional idea of Disquiet draws on the imagery of ableism, among other things, but I don't know whether it's written for players who actually experience such prejudice themselves in reality and might not be interested in a fantastic and stylized version of an actual mundane concern for them when they want to relax and have fun in a fantasy setting for a few hours.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> So where does that leave us? <br /> <br /> I would suggest that players and Storytellers could invert and modify the assumptions of Disquiet and write characters who relate to it in unexpected ways. Perhaps (a character believes/it's objectively true that) Disquiet is caused by simple human ignorance, its effects are less severe, and it doesn't actually originate from the Azoth. Perhaps your character sees Disquiet as an unfortunate fault of the human spirit, and their Pilgrimage will involve some sort of scientific/sociological/alchemical Great Work on humanity as a whole that reduces or dampens Disquiet in mystical sympathy with their own New Dawn. Maybe the onus is on humans to refine lead into gold themselves, escape their own Disquiet, and embrace Prometheans as they are. Or on a smaller scale, maybe a character's Pilgrimage isn't about somehow making themselves &quot;worthy&quot; of humanity, but constructing a life that liberates them from Disquiet by embracing their own goals, surrounding themselves with people (Created, humans, etc) who are worthy of their trust, and minimizing contact with people who will harm them.<br /> <br /> Or you could just excise Disquiet from the game entirely and see where that takes you, if your group finds that more fun! That's always on the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:38:54-07:00","id":954482,"title":"","content":"I gotta say, there are times that I wish that <i>all</i> of the mind-warping aura effects (e.g., Lunacy, Sleeping Curse, Disquiet, Sybaris) would collectively die in a fire, to be replaced with the good old-fashioned fear and prejudice that they resemble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:40:18-07:00","id":954483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet#post954321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here's the thing. Its been a while since I played Promethean its been years since the first edition came out and I played it. Now, after reading through the 2nd edition, I found myself becoming highly uncomfortable with Disquiet. Not because it isolated the Promethean, or drove them to do something, but because it felt too much like some variation on victim blaming.<br /> <br /> Prometheans are disfigured. They're a bit unbalanced mentally (unbalanced humors and all that). Fair enough. And everyone hates them because of all this - flaring disfigurements leads to more prejudice. It is literally is the Promethean's fault that everyone hates them. To me, I'm left feeling like we're just making an excuse for what amounts to prejudice and discrimination against the disabled. And I am not okay with that. <br /> <br /> I'm not the only one who feels that way, but, by the same token, there's a lot of people who feel radically different on the issue. So, here's my question. How do you feel about the issue? What do you take away from Disquiet? What do you think it means beyond a method of socially isolating the Prometheans?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have thought victim blaming fits in perfectly. It's a game about personal horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:43:37-07:00","id":954487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet#post954321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here's the thing. Its been a while since I played Promethean its been years since the first edition came out and I played it. Now, after reading through the 2nd edition, I found myself becoming highly uncomfortable with Disquiet. Not because it isolated the Promethean, or drove them to do something, but because it felt too much like some variation on victim blaming.<br /> <br /> Prometheans are disfigured. They're a bit unbalanced mentally (unbalanced humors and all that). Fair enough. And everyone hates them because of all this - flaring disfigurements leads to more prejudice. It is literally is the Promethean's fault that everyone hates them. To me, I'm left feeling like we're just making an excuse for what amounts to prejudice and discrimination against the disabled. And I am not okay with that.<br /> <br /> I'm not the only one who feels that way, but, by the same token, there's a lot of people who feel radically different on the issue. So, here's my question. How do you feel about the issue? What do you take away from Disquiet? What do you think it means beyond a method of socially isolating the Prometheans?</div> </div> </div> </div>i've got two ways to intrepret disquiet. a Literal explanation and a metaphorical explanation.<br /> <br /> The Literal explanation without any metaphors and without drawing paralles between the divine fire and anything else is that the Disquiet happens divine fire is simply too bright. and alien,it shines through the promethean dead flesh and it affects human being negavtively. Humans despites their many qualities are still fallible,and the divine fire force them to become more and more flawed. disquiet is the natural way a person feels when Pyros is close at hand,the fire fuck with their heads,even the noblest,kindest and nicest human can be cruel when affected by pyros,the same way they all burn if they touch a hot stove,they just don't have any defense agains pyros<br /> <br /> Now the metaphorical interpretation, Disquiet is a metaphor for one of humanity's greatest flaws. the fact people have a hard time relating to anyone who's different. prometheans can be allegories for autism,for other's ethnies, genders and sexualities and for disfigured people. And many humans,thought not all,react badly when face people that are like prometheans,that's what Disquiet is a a metaphor for,the human flaw of rejecting the Other until we get to know the Other. I feel like that metaphor is present mostly to showcase that despite humanity it's a desirable state,humans a whole are pretty flawed. but i don't think the text implies it's the prometean fault the disquiet is happening,i think the text is saying &quot;Disquiet happens because that just how humans are it's a intrisic flaw of the human condition,and if you want to be human you gotta understand that&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 08-20-2016, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T11:30:42-07:00","id":954508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=954332#post954332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matt, I respect you, so don't take this wrong way, but that is nothing more than quibbling over semantics and doesn't actually answer the question. No, its not the Promethean's &quot;fault&quot; anymore than someone who's born with stunted arms are at fault for being born that way, or suffering an injury in combat, or anything like that. However, unlike someone who has these actual problems in real life, the problem entirely lies within the person with the actual prejudice. Or perhaps society itself teaching the person that prejudice. But in the case of Promethean, its specifically an attribute of the Created that fucks with people's minds and <i>forces them </i>to feel that way. All these games are metaphors, and the metaphor here is that the disfigurements are at fault for making people hate you. No, its not the prejudiced person's fault, its entirely you and your body's. And I'm not okay with that.<br /> <br /> This is my interpretation of the work, and people trying to just refute how I feel about it isn't going to be constructive; rather, that has the effect of actually <i>entrenching</i> people, myself included. I'm looking to hear other interpretations and ideas, specifically because that's how I learn and grow and get new perspectives. New ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, you came up with an interpretation of part of the game, you're not interested in opinions that differ or in discussing the matter...but you want new ideas? And you're not listening to the people who made the game? (Which, like, death of the author, I get it.) OK. You're just gonna have to cope with semantic arguments, though. Words are important to me. Words mean things. The specific word choices we use mean things. So I'm gonna try this again. <br /> <br /> It is not the Promethean's fault that he engender Disquiet. It is not the human's fault that she experiences Disquiet. The human does not choose to feel it, the Promethean does not choose to engender it. If we want to look at this on a metaphorical level...actually, put a pin in that a sec, and let's talk concrete, ground-level shit for a minute. <br /> <br /> Disquiet exists within the game in order to isolate Prometheans from people and to propel a sense of, well, disquiet and, yes, othering that they go through. If they felt at ease with humanity, the Pilgrimage wouldn't make sense. If they felt superior to humanity (as, you could argue, vampires, werewolves, mages, even demons often do), the Pilgrimage wouldn't make sense. In order for the central conceit of the game (Prometheans can become human via the Pilgrimage and are driven to do so) to stand up, there has to be something driving a wedge between the Created and humanity. (Disquiet is actually fairly different than Lunacy or Disbelief in that it doesn't hide Prometheans from view; it actually does kinda the opposite.) <br /> <br /> In addition, it puts into a game-mechanic format a lot of the source material that we draw on for <b>Promethean</b>. When we think of stories about creatures like Frankenstein's monster or other artificially created beings, the revulsion and disgust that people feel (though it's expressed very different depending on what movie you're watching, as it were) is a pretty important story element. <br /> <br /> Now, to get metaphorical - I kinda see it as a play on the influence of entrenched dogma and prejudice. We are none of free of the bias of our upbringing. I had a teacher in high school who told a story about being out in traffic and having a car driven by a black man cut her off, and her first thought a &quot;damn n*****.&quot; She was horrified at herself for thinking it - she didn't consider herself racist and she certainly didn't actually feel that the man's race had anything in particular to do with his driving, but there it was. I would submit that we <i>all</i> have these biases, and that we take them out on people knowing very little about them, except for how they fit into our worldview. This is true until we learn who they really are (until they enter our Monkeysphere) and we can judge them as people. <br /> <br /> Of course, within the game, Prometheans don't even get <i>that</i>. Disquiet affects everybody, sooner or later. But one of the things I wanted to do with this edition is make Disquiet a little more forgiving; it's still inevitable, long-term, probably, but a Promethean can form a relationship with a person and enter his Monkeysphere, become a &quot;real person&quot; <i>to that particular human</i>, and in the process get a sense of what completing the Pilgrimage is likely to be like. (That is, at least, until Disquiet comes crashing down and ruins everything, because <b>Promethean</b> is pretty tragic, at least during the actual process of the Pilgrimage.)<br /> <br /> So, again, you're right: Disquiet is profoundly unfair, to both the Promethean and to the person being affected by it. You could make that argument of systemic bias and prejudice, too. Now, by learning about it, being aware of it, can you avoid or at least mitigate Disquiet, much as someone who's paying attention to their responses learn to recognize systemic bias? Sure, but how that would look in play opens up questions of who the PCs are and who's actually rolling the dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T12:37:11-07:00","id":954550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=954349#post954349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's where your metaphor breaks down for me. Because Disfigurements are only a part of what causes the Disquiet. Normal interactions also causes it, Failing a power also does. Being in your wasteland can cause such a thing too. Having a very disquieted friend can cause you to suffer disquiet.<br /> <br /> Promethean is about handicapped people, yes. But it's also about trans people, about autism, about sexuality, about homelessness, Promethean is about accepting yourself, and until then, others won't accept you.<br /> <br /> Have you ever had a friend always saying that no one loves them? That no matter what they do, they'll end up alone and sad? At first, you feel empathy, you want to help them, you give them support. Then you start to answer mechanically, without real thought. Then you start to tell them to stop complaining all the time, even if that's not really what you meant. And after some time, you need a breather, away from that person.<br /> <br /> While presiding over my game club, we've had a few people on the autism spectrum. One of them was higher on it than others. At first we tried to be inclusive, but at some point we had to have an intervention, because his presence demanded a lot from us, which we couldn't always provide.<br /> <br /> I've once met someone who has OCD about the *shhhh* sound. It caused him to get very aggressive. Like... <i>very</i> aggressive. He was expelled from college for assaulting his teacher. At first we tried our best, but once he decided to stay at the club and watch an RPG session we were playing (wihch is fine). He was on the couch, listening, basically being invisible, and at some point I roleplayed the sound of Acid melting metal, which, you guessed it, triggered him. Small events like these add up to people's tolerance of others and eventually we told him that he could either accept the noises we made in our private games or leave.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is... Disquiet is not the Promethean's fault. It's not the mortal's fault either. It's wrong alchemy between the two of them, causing the disquieted people to act out-of-character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically this. What he says is true, but underlying all of this is that the world isn't fair, especially the world of darkness. It's not the Prometheans fault that he is what he is, but its still his burden to bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T13:07:01-07:00","id":954565,"title":"","content":"One way to make it more tolerable for you could be to make a setting change. For example: An occultist or scientist knows that his time is short. They are about to be executed, assassinated, or die of a terminal illness. Maybe they are wracked with guilt and terrified of divine judgment, so they create a Promethean to be their new body after the old one dies. When this person dies, the Promethean wakes up, but lacks the memories of his former life. As the chronicle goes one, this Promethean realizes that his condition (the disquiet) is entirely his own fault. If you want to make this about a group simply make it a suicide pact cult, they can each get their own Promethean, or bits and pieces of their creators personality's can be mixed together among them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 08-20-2016, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T14:18:46-07:00","id":954611,"title":"","content":"Promethean is a game about being on the outside looking in, and trying to grasp what makes humanity so beautiful even as it shows you its worst aspects. Disquiet is a useful narrative tool to provide opposition to the player characters and reinforce that whole uncanny valley effect you get from being a corpse full of Divine Fire rather than a real person with a soul, and pairs nicely with Torment to enforce how uncomfortable things are and how much you should strive to surpass the Created condition in order to escape them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T23:13:03-07:00","id":954852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=954482#post954482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gotta say, there are times that I wish that <i>all</i> of the mind-warping aura effects (e.g., Lunacy, Sleeping Curse, Disquiet, Sybaris) would collectively die in a fire, to be replaced with the good old-fashioned fear and prejudice that they resemble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but then you don't get a world where the supernatural is hidden. You get True Blood.<br /> <br /> For me, the metaphor works specifically because the hate is part of the supernatural metaphor. When you're just applying literal prejudice to monsters, the whole thing falls apart because now your stand-in for real minorities dealing with prejudice ARE THINGS PEOPLE HAVE A COMPLETELY LOGICAL REASON TO BE SCARED OF - which makes them a terrible stand in for othered human communities.<br /> <br /> So I'll take my supernatural monsters dealing with supernatural othering over dangerous monsters dealing with the prejudice that the actually unjustly othered have to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-21-2016, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T08:54:26-07:00","id":954965,"title":"","content":"I <i>did</i> say \u201cthere are times when\u2026\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T10:02:10-07:00","id":955002,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a>, watch out, or you will be labeled transhumanist on this forum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Myself, I take Disquiet as 'Uncanny Valley' effect of Created or mystical affliction. Prometheans can be metaphor for many minorities, most important thing is that they are always Others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:22:53-07:00","id":955076,"title":"","content":"I've always thought Disquiet was a...sneaky little way to let humanity off the hook for being dicks. It's another reason why I hammer on the whole &quot;missing the point of Frankenstein&quot; thing- the book doesn't assure the reader &quot;oh, it's not the fault of those humans that they hate and fear the monster just because he's strange! A mystical magical effect made them do it!&quot;<br /> <br /> In The Lightning Chronicle, Disquiet is altered, so that its a gameplay abstraction that represents that prejudice and discomfort, rather than an actual force. This means that people not inclined to have an issue with patchwork corpses that don't quite grasp social mores don't have an issue with it, and it diminishes the more a Promethean interacts with a given person (seriously, the fact that Disquiet INCREASES the more you interact with a person is just...it just really hammers in the &quot;magical excuse&quot; thing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:09:24-07:00","id":955117,"title":"","content":"Just because people are under the influence of Disquiet doesn't mean they aren't still responsible for their actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:20:52-07:00","id":955125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955117#post955117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because people are under the influence of Disquiet doesn't mean they aren't still responsible for their actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, in the ChroD world, where pretty much everyone acknowledges on some level that there are dark dangerous deadly things lurking out there in the night, I'm not how much you can expect people to be able to resist Disquiet or penalize them for giving in. It brings me back to the post about &quot;good-old-fashioned fear and prejudice&quot;- people in ChroD are very likely to react that way to anything strange (because it will probably eat them), so when you add a magical effect that compels them to act that way...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:25:43-07:00","id":955130,"title":"","content":"I think the suggestion there is that we can accept and empathize with how fear of the unknown and unconscious bias can effect people's judgement while still holding them accountable for their actions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:31:44-07:00","id":955136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955130#post955130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the suggestion there is that we can accept and empathize with how fear of the unknown and unconscious bias can effect people's judgement while still holding them accountable for their actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I agree with that, but I'm super uncomfortable with applying the language of social justice to a tabletop setting about literal monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:35:21-07:00","id":955138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955130#post955130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the suggestion there is that we can accept and empathize with how fear of the unknown and unconscious bias can effect people's judgement while still holding them accountable for their actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I was trying to get at, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:37:38-07:00","id":955140,"title":"","content":"If that's how you want to take it, that's fine. I think it's interesting grounds for a story to explore how someone might feel about undergoing Disquiet and doing something horrible to someone they otherwise liked. Do you treat whatever ugly thoughts the Disquiet brought to the fore in you as totally external to your person and way of thinking? Or does it just shine a light on something already inside of you, so that you can't ignore it any longer?<br /> <br /> When you killed someone who defended the thing you called your friend, or you chased your daughter's strange new girlfriend away with a kitchen knife and she saw you, do you blame the Promethean? Do you internalize your behavior while you were under Disquiet and incorporate that into your personality, because confronting the idea that it <i>wasn't </i>you requires acknowledging something about the world that you'd do anything to avoid?<br /> <br /> I think people treat these situations as clear-cut because of their player-side knowledge of mechanics, but in-play, in-character, the line between &quot;you&quot; and &quot;Disquiet&quot; is likely to be a lot more blurred, much in the same way that your unconscious bias/prejudice inhabits that liminal space between conscious &quot;you&quot; and &quot;not-you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:38:06-07:00","id":955142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955136#post955136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I agree with that, but I'm super uncomfortable with applying the language of social justice to a tabletop setting about literal monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm... Why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:43:00-07:00","id":955146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955142#post955142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm... Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume because fear of something that survives by drinking people's blood (for example), or not wanting someone who creates Wastelands around, or feeling violated by the power of someone who can read your mind, scry long distance, mess with your fate - etc etc etc are all completely reasonable reactions. Unlike actually marginalized humans, the fear toward monsters is justified which creates an inherently problem with them as a stand in for the unjustly oppressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:45:47-07:00","id":955147,"title":"","content":"This was one of my biggest problems with True Blood. You can't do a civil rights or gay rights allegory, where the anti-rights side have valid points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:45:47-07:00","id":955148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955146#post955146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume because fear of something that survives by drinking people's blood (for example), or not wanting someone who creates Wastelands around, or feeling violated by the power of someone who can read your mind, scry long distance, mess with your fate - etc etc etc are all completely reasonable reactions. Unlike actually marginalized humans, the fear toward monsters is justified which creates an inherently problem with them as a stand in for the unjustly oppressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that the fear of <i>Prometheans</i> is justified, which is what we were talking about. And effects like Quiessence and Lunacy aren't metaphors for systemic predjudice like Disquiet is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:48:02-07:00","id":955152,"title":"","content":"between the effects of Wastelands and Torment, I wouldn't want one hanging around even without disquiet effecting my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:22:51-07:00","id":955172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955146#post955146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume because fear of something that survives by drinking people's blood (for example), or not wanting someone who creates Wastelands around, or feeling violated by the power of someone who can read your mind, scry long distance, mess with your fate - etc etc etc are all completely reasonable reactions. Unlike actually marginalized humans, the fear toward monsters is justified which creates an inherently problem with them as a stand in for the unjustly oppressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nail on the head. Prometheans are literally monsters, in that they're designed specifically to embody the traits of a particular horror archetype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:25:01-07:00","id":955173,"title":"","content":"Here's the main reason I don't interpret Promethean as a marginalized people allegory: that would make the end goal assimilation and erasure.<br /> <br /> Rather, as with Frankenstein, I interpret Promethean as an allegory for the entire human experience. Admittedly unlike Frankenstein, Promethean puts the root issue in our own nature than society's, but that is just keeping with philosophical shifts since the publication of Frankenstein from the romantic view of individual purity to the post-Freudian psychological view of behavior and experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-21-2016, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:31:27-07:00","id":955177,"title":"","content":"Glamourweaver's got it down pretty strongly, from my perspective. &quot;Supernatural beings as a thematic stand-in for real-life oppression&quot; is an inherently broken aesop, because there are legitimate reasons to be afraid of many supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> I mean, in all honesty, I more or less ditch the &quot;personal horror&quot; mojo in my ChrOD setting homebrews and go for something a little closer in feel to the WoD, as I'm an unabashed &quot;Humanity, Fuck YOU!&quot; supernatural fanguy. But I don't <b>hate</b> hunters as a concept because they have a perfectly natural and valid reason for existing. <br /> <br /> Vampires suck blood and can potentially drain humans dry just because they get too caught up in feeding to stop. <br /> <br /> Werewolves are predators with hyper-aggression problems. <br /> <br /> Mages, mentally, are closer to the Great Old Ones of Lovecraft than they are to humans and that's not even getting into their potential to cause huge destruction by complete accident. <br /> <br /> Faeries are an unholy amalgam of murder, rape, kidnapping and other crimes by their very nature, and even changelings can be so damaged from their experiences they can lash out unpredictably. <br /> <br /> Prometheans suffer similar bouts of hyper-aggression to werewolves and cause a literal spiritual pollution wherever they go - I don't need magical brain-whammying to object to having a leaky nuclear reactor camp out in my backyard, especially if if I know it may get pissed and try to punch my head down my neck if I politely ask it to move on before it irradiates my supply of drinking water.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters walk amongst the dead and so there's always that possibility that they'll side with the ghosts over the humans, beyond their general potential to just be a selfish dick and abuse their necromancy for their own ends... yeah, okay, this is a weak case.<br /> <br /> I could probably go on, but this gets my point across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:31:50-07:00","id":955179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955173#post955173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the main reason I don't interpret Promethean as a marginalized people allegory: that would make the end goal assimilation and erasure.<br /> <br /> Rather, as with Frankenstein, I interpret Promethean as an allegory for the entire human experience. Admittedly unlike Frankenstein, Promethean puts the root issue in our own nature than society's, but that is just keeping with philosophical shifts since the publication of Frankenstein from the romantic view of individual purity to the post-Freudian psychological view of behavior and experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here I've been playing it as a transgender metaphor for a decade now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:35:38-07:00","id":955181,"title":"","content":"I'm talking about my personal experience, if that works at the table for you, great!<br /> <br /> Of course this gets at a huge debate within the trans community about &quot;passing&quot; and cis gender role assimilation vs the importance of trans identity in its own right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:35:59-07:00","id":955182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955179#post955179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And here I've been playing it as a transgender metaphor for a decade now.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I've always thought that being trans made me feel more like a Centimani.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:40:39-07:00","id":955187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955173#post955173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the main reason I don't interpret Promethean as a marginalized people allegory: that would make the end goal assimilation and erasure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the main reason I don't interpret the New Dawn as assimilation and erasure: that would <i>cause</i> <s>dysphoria</s>Torment, not alleviate it.<br /> <br /> I've said it before and I'll say it again, the Pilgrimage is about building an identity of your own choosing, rather than the identity that was assigned to you at <s>birth</s>Creation. It's not about rejecting who you really are to become the person society wants you to be, it's about rejecting the person your <s>parents</s>Genitor wanted you to be to become who you choose to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:42:43-07:00","id":955191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955181#post955181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course this gets at a huge debate within the trans community about &quot;passing&quot; and cis gender role assimilation vs the importance of trans identity in its own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. The New Dawn isn't &quot;passing&quot; unless you want it to be. It's about building an identity that doesn't cause you Torment, what ever that identity might be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:45:43-07:00","id":955193,"title":"","content":"Except your Genitor DID make you with the goal of the New Dawn in mind (most likely). Prometheans are alchemical engines built for transformation. I don't see who the New Dawn is defying (other than Flux itself I suppose).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:46:31-07:00","id":955194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955181#post955181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about my personal experience, if that works at the table for you, great!<br /> <br /> Of course this gets at a huge debate within the trans community about &quot;passing&quot; and cis gender role assimilation vs the importance of trans identity in its own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean isn't just about &quot;boy howdy I'd love to be invisible and fit in,&quot; though. It's a game that's fundamentally about building an identity for yourself (the importance of Roles in 2e further emphasizes this, though it was already there in 1e) and trying to escape the daily hell of self-loathing that is the Torment roiling within you and the Disfigured body you constantly see. That latter bit about body stuff is especially important, as the idea that &quot;this body is literally someone else's and I would give anything to be myself&quot; is straightforward enough as to write itself.<br /> <br /> I love Promethean because it allows for a wide variety of interpretations; there was a compelling argument from someone about how they saw it as very much similar to their own experiences living as an individual on the autism spectrum, for instance. The fact that it practically screams &quot;queer identity metaphor&quot; to me says more about me as a reader than the game as a whole, but it is something that fits quite well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:46:53-07:00","id":955195,"title":"","content":"And you have no choice but to become human and mortal- that's the only kind of identity that's acceptable.<br /> <br /> And I feel like looking at it as an autism metaphor is even worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:52:11-07:00","id":955198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955195#post955195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you have no choice but to become human and mortal- that's the only kind of identity that's acceptable.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the only kind of identity that's <i>stable</i> \u2014 literally everything else on offer, <i>especially</i> the Divine Fire, can and will yank the rug out from under you at whim for the sake of what amounts to an art project.<br /> <br /> Self-realization means you stop being temperamental spell components and start being a person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:52:54-07:00","id":955200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955195#post955195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you have no choice but to become human and mortal- that's the only kind of identity that's acceptable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very literal interpretation. &quot;Human&quot; as a state of being is itself a metaphor for the state of being at peace with your identity. It's not that only certain identities are acceptable, it's that any identity that you create for yourself is metaphorically represented by the human condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-21-2016, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:57:15-07:00","id":955205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955198#post955198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the only kind of identity that's <i>stable</i> \u2014 literally everything else on offer, <i>especially</i> the Divine Fire, can and will yank the rug out from under you at whim for the sake of what amounts to an art project.<br /> <br /> Self-realization means you stop being temperamental spell components and start being a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only reason why human is the only stable identity in the Promethean universe is because the devs made it that way. I'm saying they shouldn't have. <br /> <br /> What if my identity is &quot;immortal robotic spider&quot;? You could define that as &quot;human&quot;, but Promethean sure as hell tells you you're wrong for wanting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:03:27-07:00","id":955213,"title":"","content":"I think people have a problem with reading monster fiction as being 1-to-1 with reality, which is how you get the idea of the transgressive representation of the other in monster fiction being described as a &quot;broken aesop.&quot; If the thing that it was doing was 1-to-1 with reality, there wouldn't be Disquiet, there'd just be fear &amp; prejudice, and there wouldn't be a monster, there'd be &lt;insert your favorite other here.&gt;<br /> <br /> If we accept the idea that a thing can represent another thing and not actually <b>be </b>that thing, then we're in the realm of the story. Disquiet as a mechanic is a literary device in the story of Promethean, and becoming human is not the literal, 1-to-1 transition of going from &quot;being special or being Other&quot; to being everybody else, but rather a moment of self-realization which allows one to come to terms with who they are and the baggage that they carry as a result, leaving that behind to live their life.<br /> <br /> Maybe then, Disquiet going away doesn't represent some kind of literal 1-to-1 escape of prejudice, but rather can <i>also </i>represent how our inability to come to terms with ourselves can put us in situations where a home is no longer a home, a friend is an enemy, and we feel forced to leave things behind.<br /> <br /> All of this stuff seems to rely on implicitly understanding that the fiction and the metaphor don't map exactly to reality and that a more substantial analysis than a surface comparison is more rewarding than just looking at the thing, comparing it to a piece of the puzzle, and then declaring it broken.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:04:32-07:00","id":955214,"title":"","content":"To be clear, I only meant to explain my interpretation, not suggest that anyone else's was wrong to run with for them and their group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:05:22-07:00","id":955215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955205#post955205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only reason why human is the only stable identity in the Promethean universe is because the devs made it that way. I'm saying they shouldn't have. <br /> <br /> What if my identity is &amp;quot;immortal robotic spider&amp;quot;? You could define that as &amp;quot;human&amp;quot;, but Promethean sure as hell tells you you're wrong for wanting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't do this to another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:06:53-07:00","id":955216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955205#post955205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only reason why human is the only stable identity in the Promethean universe is because the devs made it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally every other gameline in the franchise has had being a supernatural entity involve giving more of your autonomy over to supersapient primordial theme-clusters than most people would willingly default to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if my identity is &quot;immortal robotic spider&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Then you have an incredibly shallow definition of &quot;identity.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could define that as &quot;human&quot; </div> </div> </div>In Eclipse Phase, possibly, but you've purported to be fine with this game not being Eclipse Phase.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but Promethean sure as hell tells you you're wrong for wanting it. </div> </div> </div>It tells you that you're in an inherently temporary state whose most direct exit condition is the one not walled off by blood and fire and teeth and thorns. Few would prefer trying to live in a bottomless quicksand pit for the rest of their existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:12:58-07:00","id":955218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955216#post955216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally every other gameline in the franchise has had being a supernatural entity involve giving more of your autonomy over to supersapient primordial theme-clusters than most people would willingly default to.<br /> <br /> Then you have an incredibly shallow definition of &amp;quot;identity.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> In Eclipse Phase, possibly, but you've purported to be fine with this game not being Eclipse Phase.<br /> <br /> It tells you that you're in an inherently temporary state whose most direct exit condition is the one not walled off by blood and fire and teeth and thorns. Few would prefer trying to live in a bottomless quicksand pit for the rest of their existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you don't answer. This thread is about Disquiet. If everyone wants to fight about transhumanism again, please do it somewhere else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:24:52-07:00","id":955226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955193#post955193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except your Genitor DID make you with the goal of the New Dawn in mind (most likely). Prometheans are alchemical engines built for transformation. I don't see who the New Dawn is defying (other than Flux itself I suppose).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's defying the circumstances of your Creation. Yeah, a Promethean's Genitor probably created her with the goal of the New Dawn in mind. My parents birthed me with the goal of being a fulfilled person in mind. It isn't their fault that the body I was born in wasn't conducive to that end, or that the society I was born into doesn't see the identity I find fulfilling as valid. Likewise, it isn't the Genitor's fault that his Creation is subject to Torment and needs to undergo a journey of self-discovery before they'll be able to make themselves into the person they want to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:25:08-07:00","id":955227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955187#post955187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said it before and I'll say it again, the Pilgrimage is about building an identity of your own choosing, rather than the identity that was assigned to you at <s>birth</s>Creation. It's not about rejecting who you really are to become the person society wants you to be, it's about rejecting the person your <s>parents</s>Genitor wanted you to be to become who you choose to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I'd love to see a hack for <b>Promethean</b> that emphasizes this notion a bit more. P2e pp.76\u201378 feature a \u201cPostpartum\u201d section that's all about a Promethean's early days when it was still under the care of its creator, before it discovered the Pilgrimage; but this is treated entirely as Prolog. How about an \u201cearly days\u201d chronicle where the main conflict is between the young Promethean and the authority figure that's set on defining its nature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:27:20-07:00","id":955232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955227#post955227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I'd love to see a hack for <b>Promethean</b> that emphasizes this notion a bit more. P2e pp.76\u201378 feature a \u201cPostpartum\u201d section that's all about a Promethean's early days when it was still under the care of its creator, before it discovered the Pilgrimage; but this is treated entirely as Prolog. How about an \u201cearly days\u201d chronicle where the main conflict is between the young Promethean and the authority figure that's set on defining its nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be awesome! I'd love to see the idea explored in a Player's Guide or some such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:29:03-07:00","id":955234,"title":"","content":"That reminds me, relationships between Prometheans and their creators are another thing I'll have to cover in The Lightning Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:31:43-07:00","id":955235,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> \u2014 you do that. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> \u2014 Seems more like a Storyteller's Guide sort of thing to me. After all, the focus is on how to do a particular kind of Chronicle \u2014 whereas a Player's Guide is more about \u201cmore options/advice for the player\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:38:50-07:00","id":955242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955235#post955235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> \u2014 Seems more like a Storyteller's Guide sort of thing to me. After all, the focus is on how to do a particular kind of Chronicle \u2014 whereas a Player's Guide is more about \u201cmore options/advice for the player\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, good point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"