b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if my identity is &quot;immortal robotic spider&quot;? You could define that as &quot;human&quot;, but Promethean sure as hell tells you you're wrong for wanting it.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/MwW3aXx.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955215#post955215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please don't do this to another thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T16:54:52-07:00","id":955296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955002#post955002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a>, watch out, or you will be labeled transhumanist on this forum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> \u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't stir the shit pot unless you want to lick the spoon.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:33:48-07:00","id":955315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955278#post955278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/MwW3aXx.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, can we not make transphobic jokes? The attack helicopter copypasta was literally made up to mock trans people. I'm not going to argue about transhumanism in this thread, but I am going to politely ask that we not drag shitty anti-SJ memes into this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T21:32:18-07:00","id":955412,"title":"","content":"I interpret Disquiet like this: Prometheans are created beings, but they are not <i>completed</i> beings. One might almost call them &quot;quasi modo.&quot; The alchemical reactor within them does not have great containment. This makes it an amazing conduit for the Divine Fire, as it seeks the path of least resistance, but also allows the Divine Fire to leak into the world around them in its raw form. Disquiet is a side effect of the unfiltered Divine Fire touching the world in a way it normally can't, but the Promethean is not the source of the Divine Fire or the Disquiet it generates any more than you are the source of the air in your lungs.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think its too easy to get hung up on what kind of metaphor Promethean is. Focusing in on any one metaphor that's &quot;best&quot; really only serves to pigeonhole the game and limit the kinds of stories you can tell with it. You can view stories through the lens of metaphor, but it shouldn't serve the metaphor at the expense of the story. Promethean emphatically <i>is</i> a metaphor for all of those things and simultaneously emphatically <i>is</i> also literally about lightning-powered flesh-monsters. All interpretations are made poorer by the absence of the others.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To elaborate a little further on the second point. <i>Star Trek</i> would not have the enduring impact that it does today if it was just a show about spaceships. At the same time though, no one was ever going to give a shit about the show's social commentary if it weren't also an entertaining escapist fantasy about fucking spaceships.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 08-22-2016, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T21:40:43-07:00","id":955416,"title":"","content":"Why do Prometheans have to be a metaphor for something? Why can't they just be a particular type of creature inspired by created beings in literature and legend, put into a game designed to explore themes of isolation and what it means to be human? I understand that some people may identify personally with certain themes or project their own meaning onto aspects of the game and that's great, but it is a mistake to assume your interpretation of the game was intended by the designers. I can't speak for the other writers, but the parts I wrote weren't intended to reflect any real-world groups or issues, they were entirely written to serve the structure and themes of the game as laid out by the developer. Conversations with other writers never discussed parallels or metaphors, they were concerned with things like internal consistency, rewarding game play, clarity of writing, and mechanical cohesion. The rules and mechanics of the game are to serve the purpose of the game. You may disagree with how effectively they do so, but treating them as commentary on some aspect of society is a mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T21:48:33-07:00","id":955423,"title":"","content":"In the Promethean game I'm running right now the themes I've chosen to focus on are identity and individuality. That doesn't mean other themes don't work or that I consider them invalid, they just aren't essential to the Promethean metaphor I'm building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T02:47:42-07:00","id":955491,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955315#post955315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, can we not make transphobic jokes? The attack helicopter copypasta was literally made up to mock trans people. I'm not going to argue about transhumanism in this thread, but I am going to politely ask that we not drag shitty anti-SJ memes into this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the context I used it. Notice how you left out to what prompted my reply. Your character identifies as a robotic spider? That's like identifying as a AH-64 Apache. To put it simply: No, those things aren't human beings.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T03:54:42-07:00","id":955509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955416#post955416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do Prometheans have to be a metaphor for something? Why can't they just be a particular type of creature inspired by created beings in literature and legend, put into a game designed to explore themes of isolation and what it means to be human? I understand that some people may identify personally with certain themes or project their own meaning onto aspects of the game and that's great, but it is a mistake to assume your interpretation of the game was intended by the designers. I can't speak for the other writers, but the parts I wrote weren't intended to reflect any real-world groups or issues, they were entirely written to serve the structure and themes of the game as laid out by the developer. Conversations with other writers never discussed parallels or metaphors, they were concerned with things like internal consistency, rewarding game play, clarity of writing, and mechanical cohesion. The rules and mechanics of the game are to serve the purpose of the game. You may disagree with how effectively they do so, but treating them as commentary on some aspect of society is a mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Death of the author, man. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And actually, that's fine. This kind of discussion - including what <b>Promethean</b> might or might not mean in metaphorical or interpretative terms - is totally fine. While I don't tend to interpret the Pilgrimage one way or another across the board in my own games, I've certainly seen (and deliberately drawn) parallels between the difficulties that the Created have with human interaction and the difficulties that folks on the autism spectrum have with social interaction (subject to comfort discussions with players, obviously). <br /> <br /> That doesn't mean I think that <b>Promethean</b> is a metaphor for autism and learning to assimilate. I <i>do</i> think that what a couple of people have said in this thread - that the Pilgrimage is about crafting a place for yourself in the world and being able to accept yourself, and for the world to accept you - is pretty apt. <br /> <br /> 'Cause let's flip this just a sec. I'm sure we all know folks who are aggressive, arrogant, know-it-all assholes. I was one for a long time. Not only did I not cultivate empathy, I just didn't see the point. It would simplistic to say &quot;I grew up,&quot; but if I'm being honest, that's pretty much what happened. But it's not like that happened all at once, and it's not like there was one formative moment that did it. There were a number of formative moments, many of which were intensely personal and make no sense out of context, that created the person I am today, and it's a person I'm pretty happy with.<br /> <br /> (The punch line, of course, is that as people our &quot;Pilgrimage&quot; never stops - you never stop learning, you never stop growing, or if you do, that's not good. Prometheans, in that way, have it a little easier; their story ends when they reach the New Dawn, or at least becomes a radically different story.)<br /> <br /> So, it's not true to say that <b>Promethean</b> is deliberately a metaphor for anything. It's a metaphor for what you need it to be. I would humbly submit that if what you want is a game where you start as a supernatural creature and become a robotic spider, <i>this isn't the game for you</i>. And that's totally fine! I don't like D&amp;D, but I don't hang around the WotC forums telling people that I think their game about killing goblins for gold pieces would be awesomer if they introduced some kind of mechanic for semaphore. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T04:51:37-07:00","id":955525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955226#post955226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's defying the circumstances of your Creation. Yeah, a Promethean's Genitor probably created her with the goal of the New Dawn in mind. My parents birthed me with the goal of being a fulfilled person in mind. It isn't their fault that the body I was born in wasn't conducive to that end, or that the society I was born into doesn't see the identity I find fulfilling as valid. Likewise, it isn't the Genitor's fault that his Creation is subject to Torment and needs to undergo a journey of self-discovery before they'll be able to make themselves into the person they want to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a misconception about Promethean that the world wants Prometheans to be human. It doesn't, it wants them to be <i>gone</i>. The world tells Prometheans that they shouldn't be. The Pilgrimmage is the Promethean's way of telling the world &quot;Yes I should,&quot; and the New Dawn is the world blinking first. Especially now, when the New Dawn changes world to accommodate the identity the Promethean has built/discovered.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T05:14:44-07:00","id":955529,"title":"","content":"I feel like the answer to my question is &quot;Well, can you think of better ways to represent all these themes?&quot; And its more of an issue with the limits of mechanics and mediums than anything. And that's something I can accept more than before. It appears that my issue has to do with, in part, disagreement over what individual symbols mean and their arrangements.<br /> <br /> So, thank you everyone who actively contributed to the answer, especially blackhatmatt, Magnum Opus, Charlquin, Caladriu, Nicolas Milioni.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955509#post955509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Cause let's flip this just a sec. I'm sure we all know folks who are aggressive, arrogant, know-it-all assholes. I was one for a long time. Not only did I not cultivate empathy, I just didn't see the point. It would simplistic to say &quot;I grew up,&quot; but if I'm being honest, that's pretty much what happened. But it's not like that happened all at once, and it's not like there was one formative moment that did it. There were a number of formative moments, many of which were intensely personal and make no sense out of context, that created the person I am today, and it's a person I'm pretty happy with.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fun psychological fact - brains mature in a way that makes you unable to emphathize with others for a good portion of your life. I think everyone's got a bit of that aggressive, arrogant know-it-all asshole in them, because that's kind of how we all do grow up.<br /> <br /> And that ties nicely into the whole comparison of Prometheans and growing up / childhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T05:55:20-07:00","id":955538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955509#post955509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">would humbly submit that if what you want is a game where you start as a supernatural creature and become a robotic spider, <i>this isn't the game for you</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be Genius, or, potentially, Deviant (though considering Deviants are supposed to cling somewhat to humanity, I think, &quot;Immortal Robotic Spider&quot;-hood is probably the result of a bad Blowout).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Optionally, any situation where you become an Ephemeral being could have your shape/self-image morph into &quot;Robotic Spider&quot; given enough time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T09:12:31-07:00","id":955633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955416#post955416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do Prometheans have to be a metaphor for something? Why can't they just be a particular type of creature inspired by created beings in literature and legend, put into a game designed to explore themes of isolation and what it means to be human? I understand that some people may identify personally with certain themes or project their own meaning onto aspects of the game and that's great, but it is a mistake to assume your interpretation of the game was intended by the designers. I can't speak for the other writers, but the parts I wrote weren't intended to reflect any real-world groups or issues, they were entirely written to serve the structure and themes of the game as laid out by the developer. Conversations with other writers never discussed parallels or metaphors, they were concerned with things like internal consistency, rewarding game play, clarity of writing, and mechanical cohesion. The rules and mechanics of the game are to serve the purpose of the game. You may disagree with how effectively they do so, but treating them as commentary on some aspect of society is a mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm clapping for this. To me, ChroD lines are primarily about exploring monster archetypes, and metaphors and parallels are used to enhance that- they come second, not first. Now, I obviously don't agree with some of the ways ChroD has handled those explorations, but I consider it to be a good guiding principle, and I agree with Eric on that. <br /> <br /> For example, I consider Demon to be the best ChroD line for SJ/transition/disability readings, but that's because I know it wasn't deliberately constructed for that. It was designed to create a coherent mythology and personal exploration of the archetypes of the &quot;fallen angel&quot;, &quot;reality enforcer&quot;, and &quot;technological menace&quot;, and taking the features of those stories to their logical conclusions created something that speaks to me as a disabled trans person. If the game had basically been saying &quot;demons are just like gay/trans/disabled people! It's a metaphor!&quot; it wouldn't have worked, but it works because the theme of establishing and fighting for your own identity emerges organically from the exploration of the archetype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T09:18:14-07:00","id":955637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955509#post955509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Death of the author, man. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And actually, that's fine. This kind of discussion - including what <b>Promethean</b> might or might not mean in metaphorical or interpretative terms - is totally fine. While I don't tend to interpret the Pilgrimage one way or another across the board in my own games, I've certainly seen (and deliberately drawn) parallels between the difficulties that the Created have with human interaction and the difficulties that folks on the autism spectrum have with social interaction (subject to comfort discussions with players, obviously). <br /> <br /> That doesn't mean I think that <b>Promethean</b> is a metaphor for autism and learning to assimilate. I <i>do</i> think that what a couple of people have said in this thread - that the Pilgrimage is about crafting a place for yourself in the world and being able to accept yourself, and for the world to accept you - is pretty apt. <br /> <br /> 'Cause let's flip this just a sec. I'm sure we all know folks who are aggressive, arrogant, know-it-all assholes. I was one for a long time. Not only did I not cultivate empathy, I just didn't see the point. It would simplistic to say &amp;quot;I grew up,&amp;quot; but if I'm being honest, that's pretty much what happened. But it's not like that happened all at once, and it's not like there was one formative moment that did it. There were a number of formative moments, many of which were intensely personal and make no sense out of context, that created the person I am today, and it's a person I'm pretty happy with.<br /> <br /> (The punch line, of course, is that as people our &amp;quot;Pilgrimage&amp;quot; never stops - you never stop learning, you never stop growing, or if you do, that's not good. Prometheans, in that way, have it a little easier; their story ends when they reach the New Dawn, or at least becomes a radically different story.)<br /> <br /> So, it's not true to say that <b>Promethean</b> is deliberately a metaphor for anything. It's a metaphor for what you need it to be. I would humbly submit that if what you want is a game where you start as a supernatural creature and become a robotic spider, <i>this isn't the game for you</i>. And that's totally fine! I don't like D&amp;D, but I don't hang around the WotC forums telling people that I think their game about killing goblins for gold pieces would be awesomer if they introduced some kind of mechanic for semaphore. </div> </div> </div> </div>The spider thing was me pointing out that, for a game about creating an identity, it has a rather narrow and arbitrary definition of acceptable identity. Personally, I'd rather it be a game about starting as a supernatural creature and learning how to handle being a supernatural creature, and I see no reason why Promethean can't be that. To me, it's what it always should have been, so that's what I'm working on. Also, actually, Genius and Deviant don't fit becoming a robotic spider anywhere near as well as Demon does. Demon is awesome. <br /> <br /> And Malus? That doesn't change the fact that that joke was created to mock trans people. You can't divorce things from their origins. If you had used a racist joke to mock me, I would have called you on it. Even though I'm white and you might have thought you weren't using it in a racist way, it would still be something with a racist origin, and using it in any way keeps it in power. <br /> <br /> And not only were you using a transphobic and somewhat ableist joke, you were using it to mock a disabled trans person for saying something did not speak to them as a disabled trans person. So yes, you were being transphobic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:40:59-07:00","id":955687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955509#post955509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(The punch line, of course, is that as people our &quot;Pilgrimage&quot; never stops - you never stop learning, you never stop growing, or if you do, that's not good. Prometheans, in that way, have it a little easier; their story ends when they reach the New Dawn, or at least becomes a radically different story.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This raises an interesting question for me. Could Promethean still work if the Pilgrimage was an ongoing process, with the New Dawn as more of a semi-mythical goal than something that was known to be possible and to have been accomplished by others?<br /> <br /> This may be a little off-topic, so maybe I'll start a new one. But in a lot of ways, I think Extempore do what I like most about Promethean better than the Lineages do, and I wonder if a setting hack where all Prometheans were essentially Extempore would be worth exploring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:43:47-07:00","id":955691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955687#post955687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This raises an interesting question for me. Could Promethean still work if the Pilgrimage was an ongoing process, with the New Dawn as more of a semi-mythical goal than something that was known to be possible and to have been accomplished by others?<br /> <br /> This may be a little off-topic, so maybe I'll start a new one. But in a lot of ways, I think Extempore do what I like most about Promethean better than the Lineages do, and I wonder if a setting hack where all Prometheans were essentially Extempore would be worth exploring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you should say that, since that's exactly how the Pilgrimage works in The Lightning Chronicle. But it is off topic, so I'll be in the other thread if you make it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:21:51-07:00","id":955726,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bGecko, stop promoting your fan project in almost every post you make. Make your own thread about it in the appropriate forum and keep any conversation regarding it there. The same directive applies to anyone else that wishes to talk about fan projects. Thank you.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:21:06-07:00","id":955838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955637#post955637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The spider thing was me pointing out that, for a game about creating an identity, it has a rather narrow and arbitrary definition of acceptable identity. Personally, I'd rather it be a game about starting as a supernatural creature and learning how to handle being a supernatural creature, and I see no reason why Promethean can't be that. To me, it's what it always should have been, so that's what I'm working on. Also, actually, Genius and Deviant don't fit becoming a robotic spider anywhere near as well as Demon does. Demon is awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree that &quot;human&quot; is in any way narrow and arbitrary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:42:20-07:00","id":955858,"title":"","content":"It is in a setting with numerous supernatural creatures, especially since Promethean defines human to exclude immortality. But again, this is way offtopic and not relevant to the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T16:12:26-07:00","id":955957,"title":"","content":"I think it's another situation of conflating a scientific or technical definition of being human with a more literary and broad definition.<br /> <br /> Kind of like how &quot;the human condition&quot; might still applicably describe the situations or difficulties faced by the Kindred even though they no longer fit the game's technical definition of a human/mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T16:16:15-07:00","id":955961,"title":"","content":"Again, we probably shouldn't be keeping this argument going on a thread about Disquiet, and I'm sorry for starting and contributing to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T22:19:16-07:00","id":956159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955529#post955529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the answer to my question is &quot;Well, can you think of better ways to represent all these themes?&quot; And its more of an issue with the limits of mechanics and mediums than anything. And that's something I can accept more than before. It appears that my issue has to do with, in part, disagreement over what individual symbols mean and their arrangements.<br /> <br /> So, thank you everyone who actively contributed to the answer, especially blackhatmatt, Magnum Opus, Charlquin, Caladriu, Nicolas Milioni.<br /> <br /> Fun psychological fact - brains mature in a way that makes you unable to emphathize with others for a good portion of your life. I think everyone's got a bit of that aggressive, arrogant know-it-all asshole in them, because that's kind of how we all do grow up.<br /> <br /> And that ties nicely into the whole comparison of Prometheans and growing up / childhood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yer welcome bro","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:29:36-07:00","id":956449,"title":"","content":"I have MS, I have trouble focusing enough to watch a half hour anime episode,<br /> <br /> My mom lectured me last week for going on a walk without my cane...<br /> <br /> I find nothing Offensive whatsoever towards the disabled, in Disquiet<br /> <br /> I DO think a question worth asking is &quot;how can a Promethean use a mortal Retainer&quot;<br /> <br /> do they suddenly become immune to disquiet and it wasnt mentioned in the book or ideas on how to make use of them without engendering disquiet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:41:01-07:00","id":956458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=956449#post956449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I DO think a question worth asking is &quot;how can a Promethean use a mortal Retainer&quot;<br /> <br /> do they suddenly become immune to disquiet and it wasnt mentioned in the book or ideas on how to make use of them without engendering disquiet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disquiet is now a lot softer, so you could say that your Retainer suffers from it, but keeps doing the job because you pay them well enough. Or maybe you only contact them through phone calls and emails. Maybe they simply have enough willpower to stave off the effects, or maybe you deal with them only once or twice every month, making sure the disquiet never truly sets in.<br /> <br /> Plenty of options, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T12:03:41-07:00","id":956474,"title":"","content":"As long as the Promethean doesn't interact with their Retainer in a wasteland, it won't advance past Stage 2, which is just a -2 penalty to social rolls, +2 Doors, and no 10-again unless the player chooses to escalate it further for a Beat. And if they do have to interact with the Retainer in a Wasteland, or opt to take a Beat, there's always Sanctity of Merits. I could easily see a Promethean going through Retainer after Retainer, hiring new help each time the previous one succumbs to Disquiet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T18:00:40-07:00","id":956661,"title":"","content":"And possibly having a VERY generous Vacation and Benefits plan for his retainers, to help keep them loyal.<br /> <br /> Whats it like just curious going on vacation for a few months then meeting the promethean again after the disquiets dissipated?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T22:02:13-07:00","id":956781,"title":"","content":"\u201cThat was refreshing; let's get back to work! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u201d \u2026 \u201c\u2026now I remember why I needed that vacation\u2026\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T10:58:35-07:00","id":969321,"title":"","content":"oh a question?<br /> <br /> on a Unfleshed. when Disquiet has faded will the person forget that he was an object?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T11:46:44-07:00","id":970075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=954323#post954323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not the Promethean's &quot;fault&quot; that they engender Disquiet. It's something that they can't help. There's no moral judgement implied by it, it's just the unfortunate reaction between the Divine Fire and...basically everything else, but human perceptions in this specific case.<br /> <br /> It is, however, profoundly unfair, that much is true.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that unfairness is important for the themes of Promethian: The Created. Battling for purpose to avoid ennui caused by an uncaring world set against you is fairly fundamental, and Disquiet is a major part of that. Promethian is brave enough a game to deal with really unpleasant emotions like isolation, alienation, frustration, hate, and despair and without mechanical teeth (ie the mechanics of Disquiet) that part of the experience can simply be ignored, which is something that is natural to do. People ignore unpleasantness, people are repelled by ugliness, and people hate that which is contemptible to them. Am I talking about the people playing the game or people in the game? Both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T13:12:13-07:00","id":974628,"title":"","content":"I've always liked disquiet and personally preferred it when it was more potent because of how I view the game. No metaphors. For me Promethean has always been a game about playing a monster that does NOT belong and should not exist. So of course they get unfair treatment and suffer for just existing, they're an abomination and them reaching the New Dawn is a miracle more or less. I've always felt that the number of prommies that have achieved their Great Work are so small that maybe only one or two prometheans in the whole world manage to reach the last few steps of their pilgrimage each year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5604-faster-than-fedex","name":"Faster-Than-FedEx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T18:00:54-07:00","id":975747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=969321#post969321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh a question?<br /> <br /> on a Unfleshed. when Disquiet has faded will the person forget that he was an object?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Disquieted will probably justify it. &quot;I was under a lot of stress at the time, and it was more important that the task get finished than it was for me to play nice.&quot; People treat each other like shit and tell themselves they're in the right, even when they were consciously at their worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}